{
  "name": "Encorp | Homework | Week 03 | HW 05 | Support Ticket Router Review",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Support Ticket Router - 2/2 Review & Process (Week 03 / HW 05)\nReview Form -> Load Ticket -> Ticket Is Pending? -> Apply Review -> Mark Reviewed -> Log Review To Audit Sheet -> Support Agent (+ Append Ticket To Sheet, Create Google Task) -> Tools Succeeded? -> Mark Processed | Mark Failed -> form completion page.\nStarted by the human: the reviewer opens the link from the e-mail of workflow 1/2 (Intake) and submits the form.\n\n**Coverage:** R4 (part 2) Review Form + Apply Review + Mark Reviewed: the confirmed or changed category is written into the ticket data (the item and the Data Table row) | R5 Support Agent | R6 Append Ticket To Sheet (tab Tickets) | R7 Create Google Task.\n**State machine (Data Table support_tickets):** pending_review (Intake) -> reviewed (Mark Reviewed) -> processed | failed.\n\n**What changed vs. the first plan, and why**\n- Two workflows with a Data Table instead of Send and Wait: nothing waits inside n8n and the human has no deadline. See the note in workflow 1/2 for the planned reminder workflow (not built).\n- Duplicate guard: Load Ticket finds only rows with status pending_review, and Mark Reviewed filters on it too. A second submit shows \"not found or already reviewed\" and nothing runs twice (no second task, no second Sheet row).\n- The original is kept: sentimentAi stays in the Data Table row and in the Audit Log tab (Sentiment AI / Sentiment Final / Changed / Reviewed At). The Tickets tab has only the 5 columns required by the task, with the final category.\n- Sheet nodes use Cell Format RAW, so ticket text starting with = or + is not turned into a formula.\n- Sheets tool: date, ticket text, category and department are copied from the data by expressions (exact copy); the agent only supplies the proposed answer ($fromAI). Tasks tool: title and notes come from the agent ($fromAI).\n- The agent must start its answer with TOOL ERROR if a tool failed; Tools Succeeded then routes to Mark Failed, so the status never says processed by mistake.\n\n**Setup:** connect OpenRouter, Google Sheets (tabs Tickets and Audit Log, headers in test-data) and Google Tasks credentials | create Data Table support_tickets | publish this workflow (the form link works only in production; in test mode type the Ticket ID by hand) | the Task List is @default (your default list) - pick another in the dropdown if needed.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 1900,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        -620
      ],
      "id": "da19acff-73a9-4ccc-8fdc-d9796046d175",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview"
    },
